# --- Raw source data -------------------------------------------------------
# Excluded because it is third-party data we do not own and should not vendor:
# it is fetched from a pinned upstream commit by `make data`, which makes the
# repo reproducible without redistributing someone else's dataset under our
# name. Keeping it out also keeps raw inputs immutable -- the only way to
# change them is to change the pinned SHA in src/schema.py -- and keeps the
# clone small (~36 MB of Parquet, most of it the 20.9M-row promotions table).
data/raw/
# ...but the provenance note must survive a clone.
!data/raw/README.md

# Derived database. Rebuildable from data/raw via `make ingest`; a 92 MB
# binary that changes wholesale on every load has no business in git.
data/processed/*.duckdb
data/processed/*.duckdb.wal

# --- Tableau ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Extracts and packaged workbooks embed a copy of the data. The .twb workbook
# XML is committed; anything carrying data with it is not.
*.hyper
*.tde
*.twbx

# --- Outputs ---------------------------------------------------------------
# outputs/extracts/ IS committed -- see the note in that directory's README.
# Model binaries are not: they are large, they are tied to the exact
# scikit-learn version that wrote them, and they are regenerable.
outputs/models/*.pkl
outputs/models/*.joblib
# Generated diagnostic plots — rebuildable, not versioned.
outputs/figures/*.png
outputs/figures/*.pdf
outputs/plots/*.png
outputs/plots/*.pdf

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Jupyter ---------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- OS / IDE --------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
